sentences.text:
It is stated that the requirement of the petitioner is not bonafide; that the property bearing no. F-14/60- 61 is a huge one admeasuring 910 square yards (excluding the tenanted shop); that there are already two shops on the ground floor of property bearing no. F-14/60-61, which are lying vacant along with halls on the upper floors which can be utilized by the petitioner for her purported need; that a board with "Space Available for Rent" is hanging on these vacant shops;
that petitioner has concealed the true position of the property by not filing the complete site plan; that the area under occupation of the respondent is merely 200 square feet (8' RC ARC No. 23/2023 Inderjeet Kaur Vs. Anil Kumar Singhal Page no.
5 of 25 x 25') as evidenced from the site plan of earlier eviction proceedings and wrongly mentioned in the present petition to be 270 square feet;
that a beauty parlor cannot be run from such a small space in which a kirana shop is being run; that petitioner has no experience to run a beauty parlor and that she has not even stated her need to be bonafide.

6. In support of his application, respondent has relied upon old rent receipts and challans (supra);
copy of eviction petition filed by Mohan Bir against the respondent and his family members in 2001;
site plan; copy of rent receipt issued by United State Agency to Kwality Bazar alongwith its GST details; some photographs of property in question as well as of petitioner's property namely Paradise; photographs of respondent's shop etc.
